    "what_this_means": "This was a clean win against a real team, but the story is binary: five runs in the second, three in the sixth, and nothing in between except empty swings. Campusano drove in three, and Machado went 3-for-4, but the offense didn't sustain a thing. They got their chances early and buried Milwaukee before the lineup had to do anything again. Walker Buehler held the line for six innings. Three hits, one run, five strikeouts. Which meant the bullpen barely had to work. Peralta and Canning combined for three scoreless innings to close it. The math is simple: get ahead fast, let the starter manage, lean on relief. It worked tonight. The question is whether it works when the lineup can't detonate early.",
